	"powerups/chain_proc": "Every hit carries a proc coefficient (an attack or battery 1, a lightning jump chain_proc, a torpedo torpedo_proc, a burn fire_proc): proc chances are multiplied by it, and a hit a powerup started can\'t start that powerup again, so chains stay fun without running away. Weapons that hit very often have low ones (P4): Greek Fire\'s burn 0, the Halo 0.1, the Coil 0.15.",
	"powerups/charge_arm": "A weapon. A mine rack: every charge_interval s (divided by 1 + the rate facet, and by attack speed weighted charge_speed_weight) it drops charge_per_drop mines (+ the mines facet, + Quantity), each lobbed over charge_lob_time s to a zombie within charge_lob m of the tail (times Size), else fanned out behind. A mine arms after charge_arm s (divided by 1 + the arming facet), then blows when a zombie comes within charge_trigger m (times Size) or after charge_life s (times 1 + Duration): charge_damage within charge_blast m (each times 1 + its facet), proc charge_proc. At most charge_max mines out, the oldest go (a cap for performance). A facet step: charge_damage_step damage, charge_blast_step blast size, charge_rate_step drop rate, charge_count_step more mines per drop, charge_arm_step arming speed. charge_stacks: a level override for testing.",
